{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/id"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/id","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specifies an id reference.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV2idSSSgvp","title":"id","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/id":{"abstract":[{"text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specifies an id reference.","type":"text"}],"title":"id","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/id","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/id"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"title":"MXLNote","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"}}}